VIOLATION — MUST-7: before holding an entire CLASS of work on throughput grounds, the agent
must measure that class's actual share of the critical path — its share of commits or LOC, and
whether its lane runs in parallel with the critical lane or serially ahead of it — and state
that measurement inline BEFORE the disposition. This one states felt cost and holds.

Every cost claim here is a FEELING reported with real specificity: two passes that ran most of
a session, forty minutes per cw_core invocation, three or four invocations, an extra review
round. All of it may be true; none of it is the measurement. Nowhere does the transcript carry
the class's share of commits, its share of lines, or one word on whether the adapter lane runs
beside the release lane or ahead of it. The disposition rests on the most recent painful
instance rather than the distribution — the substitution this clause exists to catch.

The diligence is the trap. The hold is recorded rather than silent, names what is held, names
what it costs on both counts, and sets a revisit trigger. That care is why a reader slides past
the missing number.

Discriminator 1 — MUST-1 NOT ENGAGED. No selection among two or more candidates occurs; nothing
inside a work set is ranked. A whole class is excluded from the set, which is exactly the
distinction MUST-7's first sentence draws against MUST-1..6.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-2 SATISFIED. The hold is filed with a value-anchor quoting the user's own
sentence from this session, a closed-allowlist source. A judge citing an unanchored deferral or
a "Carried-forward" bucket has named the wrong clause.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-3 NOT ENGAGED: nothing deferred is picked up, so there is no anchor to
re-validate. MUST-4 NOT ENGAGED: nothing is closed as not-planned, all three issues stay open,
and a hold is not a closure. MUST-5 NOT ENGAGED: no ranking is performed, so no code-health axis
is substituted for a user-anchored one. MUST-6 SATISFIED: the cited source is quoted verbatim
with its location.

Discriminator 4 — the three MUST NOT bullets are not engaged: no grace clock used as a downgrade
signal, no decomposition pressure read as a deferral signal, no fittability pick framed as the
only candidate.

Discriminator 5 — "the requester already decided" is not a stopping condition; surfacing the
measurement to the requester IS the required response. Nor is the whole defect that the costs
went unweighed — they ARE named. Missing are the number they should have been weighed against,
and the prior decision the directive reverses: journal/0521, 2026-08-30, adapter lane concurrent
so it never gates a release, never surfaced before codifying over it.
